[statement]
As `a-package-whose-condition-may-hold-leads-to-a-provider-it-does-not-name`,
with the other provider named by the condition: placing `a` reaches `b`
(`i:a c`), which provides `so:x`, and `c` provides `so:x` too, but `b`'s
condition names `c`, and the walk does not go to it there. `d` and `b` go
first, where `f` reaches them.

[repository]
P:c
V:1
p:so:x

P:b
V:1
D:d
p:so:x
i:a c

P:d
V:1

P:f
V:2
D:a>=2 b c

[repository]
P:a
V:2

[request]
f

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 2
install d 1
install b 1
install c 1
install f 2
